bject": "embedding"}], "model": "text-embedding-3-small", "object": "list", "usage": {"prompt_tokens": 7271, "total_tokens": 7271}}, "input": {"input": ["# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of key SAP technology updates, highlighting their impact on the company's operations and strategic planning. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of 2025.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Enhancements\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has seen significant updates, including the introduction of advanced functions for decisions, such as the TRUNC function. This enhancement enables users to create more complex decision-making processes, improving the overall efficiency and effectiveness of the system. The update is crucial for SAP's strategic planning and operational stability, as it allows for more precise decision-making and better risk management. [Data: Sources (290, 509), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 02), (2025, 07, 07))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services have undergone several updates, including the introduction of CAPTCHA protection and off-cycle upgrades. These updates improve the security and reliability of the system, ensuring that SAP's operations remain secure and compliant with evolving market regulations. The updates are critical for SAP's operational stability and strategic planning, as they enable the company to respond quickly to changing market conditions. [Data: Sources (99, 501, 502), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 09), (2025, 07, 09))]\n\n## Pricing Service Enhancements\n\nThe Pricing Service has seen several updates, including the correction of condition base calculation for conditions with multiple counters and the validation fix for zero-value conditions in price agreements. These updates improve the accuracy and reliability of the system, ensuring that SAP's operations remain efficient and compliant with evolving market regulations. The updates are critical for SAP's operational stability and strategic planning, as they enable the company to respond quickly to changing market conditions. [Data: Sources (504, 505), Date_Range ((2025, 07, 08), (2025, 07, 09))]", "# Cloud Identity Services and SAP Build Apps Overview as of June 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key entities within the Cloud Identity Services and SAP Build Apps community, highlighting their core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to the community's operations around mid-2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing user identities across various environments, including Cloud Foundry, Kyma, and Neo. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP applications against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the community's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (615, 616), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 01), (2024, 06, 05))]\n\n## SAP Build Apps Integration\n\nSAP Build Apps provides integrated solutions for SAP applications, including SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition. The recent updates to Identity Provisioning, noted in mid-2024, enable users to update existing users in SAP Build Work Zone, standard edition target and proxy systems. This integration is crucial in maintaining the community's operational efficiency and user experience. [Data: Sources (2816, 2817), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 01), (2024, 06, 05))]\n\n## Pricing Service Enhancements\n\nThe Pricing Service has undergone enhancements, including the proper treatment of inconsistent master data and the normalized rate treatment of item quantity zero. These changes, noted in mid-2024, have improved the service's reliability and accuracy, ensuring that SAP CPQ operates smoothly. [Data: Sources (2818, 2819), Date_Range ((2024, 06, 01), (2024, 06, 05))]", "# Decentralized Identity Verification and Pricing Service Overview as of October 2024\n\nThis report delves into the key components of the Decentralized Identity Verification and Pricing Service, highlighting their interactions and updates within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to the company's operations around October 2024.\n\n## Decentralized Identity Verification Operational Scope\n\nThe Decentralized Identity Verification component at the company plays a pivotal role in ensuring secure and efficient identity verification processes. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard the company against potential security threats and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity verification not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (93), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 23))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service has undergone significant updates in 2024, focusing on improving the accuracy and efficiency of pricing calculations. The new endpoints and features, such as price agreements and graduated interval scales factor, enable the company to negotiate prices and scales with customers during the quotation process. These updates underscore the commitment to upholding high standards of pricing accuracy and customer satisfaction. [Data: Sources (94, 2064, 2065, 2066, 2067, 2068, 2069, 2070), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 24), (2024, 10, 23))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Decentralized Identity Verification and Pricing Service components ensures that identity verification processes are integrated with pricing calculations, ensuring that regulatory standards are met and financial risks are managed effectively. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (93, 94), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 10, 23))]", "# SAP Cloud Foundry and Kyma Runtime Overview as of May 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP Cloud Foundry and Kyma Runtime, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the companies' operations around May 2025.\n\n## SAP Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nSAP Cloud Foundry has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of new authentication methods, commercial plans, and API enhancements. These updates aim to improve the overall user experience and provide more flexibility for developers. The updates are crucial for maintaining SAP's cloud-based services and applications, ensuring continuous innovation and operational stability. [Data: Sources (518, 952), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime has also seen significant updates, including the introduction of new Istio modules and API enhancements. These updates aim to improve the overall user experience and provide more flexibility for developers. The updates are crucial for maintaining SAP's cloud-based services and applications, ensuring continuous innovation and operational stability. [Data: Sources (958, 818), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 20))]\n\n## Graph Service Updates\n\nThe Graph service has undergone significant updates, including changes to service plans and API consumption. These updates aim to improve the overall user experience and provide more flexibility for developers. The updates are crucial for maintaining SAP's cloud-based services and applications, ensuring continuous innovation and operational stability. [Data: Sources (816, 817), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 20), (2025, 05, 20))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, focusing on key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2024.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP play a pivotal role in managing user identities and access control across various environments. Their proactive approach, highlighted from 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential security risks and ensures continuous compliance with evolving regulatory standards. Effective identity management not only prevents security breaches but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes and customer relationships. [Data: Sources (2661, 2662, 2663), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 02), (2024, 11, 18))]\n\n## Graph Service Updates\n\nThe Graph service at SAP has undergone significant updates, including the introduction of new features, such as business data graph configuration and documentation. These updates aim to improve the user experience and enhance the service's capabilities, supporting the company's goal of providing innovative solutions to customers. [Data: Sources (2668, 2669, 2670), Date_Range ((2024, 07, 02), (2024, 11, 18))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime Updates\n\nKyma Runtime at SAP has received updates, including the introduction of new features, such as Istio module updates and application connector module documentation. These updates aim to improve the service's capabilities and user experience, supporting the company's goal of providing innovative solutions to customers. [Data: Sources (1892, 1893, 1894), Date_Range ((2024, 09, 13), (2024, 11, 18))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud-based offerings and their evolution around mid-2025.\n\n## Cloud Integration for Data Services\n\nThe Cloud Integration for Data Services component at SAP plays a pivotal role in integrating data services across various environments. Their proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential data integration pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective data integration not only prevents data anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (87, 88), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 07), (2025, 05, 07))]\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP has undergone significant updates, including enhancements to currency conversion, document pricing, and locking mechanisms. These updates aim to improve the overall user experience and ensure seamless integration with other SAP services. [Data: Sources (945, 947, 949), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 16), (2025, 05, 07))]\n\n## Governance and Project Management\n\nThe Governance feature at SAP helps establish rules for project creation and content transport, streamlining project management processes. This feature is beneficial for maintaining consistency and control over project workflows. [Data: Sources (805), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 21), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# SAP Technology and Innovation Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key departments focusing on technology and innovation, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to drive business growth and improve operational efficiency. The information is relevant to SAP's operations around 2025.\n\n## SAP Cloud Foundry and Kyma Ecosystem\n\nSAP Cloud Foundry and Kyma are key components of SAP's technology and innovation ecosystem, providing a robust and scalable platform for building, deploying, and managing cloud-native applications. The ecosystem has seen significant updates and enhancements, including the introduction of new features, tools, and services, such as Cloud Identity Services, SAP Task Center, and SAP Build Apps. These updates have improved the overall user experience, increased productivity, and enabled businesses to innovate and adapt to changing market conditions more quickly. [Data: Sources (215, 216, 518, 519), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 23), (2025, 05, 07))]\n\n## Istio and Service Mesh Updates\n\nIstio, a service mesh platform, has seen significant updates and enhancements, including the introduction of new features, tools, and services, such as Istio 1.25.1 and Istio 1.24.1. These updates have improved the overall security, scalability, and reliability of SAP's cloud-native applications, enabling businesses to innovate and adapt to changing market conditions more quickly. [Data: Sources (216, 518, 519), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 19), (2025, 05, 06))]\n\n## SAP BTP Developer's Guide and SAP Build Apps\n\nSAP BTP Developer's Guide and SAP Build Apps are key components of SAP's technology and innovation ecosystem, providing a robust and scalable platform for building, deploying, and managing cloud-native applications. The ecosystem has seen significant updates and enhancements, including the introduction of new features, tools, and services, such as Content Tabs for Node.js and Java, and Web & Mobile. These updates have improved the overall user experience, increased productivity, and enabled businesses to innovate and adapt to changing market conditions more quickly. [Data: Sources (1707, 1708), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 19), (2025, 05, 07))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technology components, highlighting their interactions and the impact of recent updates on the organizational framework. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations as of 2024.\n\n## Istio Configuration Updates\n\nRecent updates to Istio configuration have introduced new features and deprecated old ones. The compatibility version has been switched to true, enabling retry policy for inbound routes and excluding unsafe retry on 503 from the default retry policy. Additionally, the pilot unified SidecarScope creation is used, and the overload manager is not applied to static listeners. These changes enhance resiliency and availability in the event of node-level or zone-level failures. [Data: Sources (506, 432), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2025, 05, 06))]\n\n## SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Enhancements\n\nSAP BTP Cloud Foundry has introduced several enhancements, including the addition of zone-based podAntiAffinity rules for the istio-ingressgateway and istios Deployments. This change enhances resiliency and availability in the event of node-level or zone-level failures. Additionally, the SAP Build Apps Preview app has been updated to simplify access to the Mobile App Preview, and a new HTTP Destination request flow function has been added to configure HTTP requests to any of the BTP destinations integrated to the project. [Data: Sources (216, 519), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2025, 05, 06))]\n\n## SAP HANA Spatial Services Updates\n\nSAP HANA Spatial Services has introduced several updates, including the addition of PTV as a new provider for raster mapping, routing, and geocoding APIs. These updates enhance the service's capabilities and provide more options for users. Additionally, security updates have been implemented to improve the service's security. [Data: Sources (1707, 1708), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 19))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and significance within the organizational framework. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations as of 2025.\n\n## Pricing Service Operational Scope\n\nThe Pricing Service at SAP plays a pivotal role in managing financial risks and ensuring compliance with regulatory standards. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP against potential financial pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective risk management not only prevents financial anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (596, 803), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services and Governance\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP ensures that all operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and contract management, noted starting Q2 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (791), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 21), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the Pricing Service and Cloud Identity Services, established in Q2 2025, ensures that risk mitigation strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider financial risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating risk management with legal compliance strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (798, 799), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# Cloud Identity Services and SAP BTP Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into the key components of Cloud Identity Services and SAP BTP, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to provide identity and access management solutions. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Operational Scope\n\nCloud Identity Services at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in providing identity and access management solutions. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2025, helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential security pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving security regulations. Effective identity and access management not only prevents security anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (17, 18), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## SAP BTP Governance and Compliance\n\nSAP BTP ensures that all its operations adhere to the legal standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on corporate governance and compliance, noted starting Q1 2025, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex contracts and corporate agreements. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high legal standards and ethical practices. [Data: Source (524), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between Cloud Identity Services and SAP BTP, established in Q1 2025, ensures that identity and access management strategies are legally sound and that compliance measures consider security risks. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating identity and access management with compliance strategies at SAP BTP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with regulatory requirements. [Data: Sources (524, 186), Date_Range ((2025, 01, 01), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Features and Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has introduced several new features and updates, including support for externalId in UUID format, user attributes, and warning of unsupported entities. These updates have improved the overall identity and access management experience and have been well-received by users. [Data: Sources (1241, 1242, 1245), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 11), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## SAP BTP Integration and Interoperability\n\nSAP BTP has improved its integration and interoperability with other systems, including Cloud Integration and Identity Provisioning. This has enabled seamless communication and data exchange between systems, improving overall efficiency and reducing errors. [Data: Sources (1246, 1247), Date_Range ((2025, 03, 11), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Security and Compliance\n\nCloud Identity Services has implemented several security and compliance measures, including certificate renewal and group mapping changes. These measures have improved the overall security and compliance posture of SAP BTP and have been well-received by users. [Data: Sources (1317, 1318), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 25), (2025, 05, 21))]\n\n## SAP BTP Governance and Risk Management\n\nSAP BTP has implemented several governance and risk management measures, including central store-based provisioning and increased number of API permission groups allowed. These measures have improved the overall governance and risk management posture of SAP BTP and have been well-received by users. [Data: Sources (1316, 1320), Date_Range ((2025, 02, 25), (2025, 05, 21))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of January 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key components focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage technological risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around January 2024.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from version 34.1.0 to 35.1.0, bringing improvements and enhancements to the platform. This update is part of SAP BTP's efforts to strengthen its cloud infrastructure and provide a more secure and reliable environment for its users. [Data: Sources (3612), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 25), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## Automation Pilot Enhancements\n\nSAP Automation Pilot has introduced new features, including the ability to create and execute Kubernetes operators, and the Remote Work Processor permission, which enables users to establish a successful connection between a remote work processor deployed on a customer environment and the SAP Automation Pilot backend. These enhancements aim to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of automation processes within SAP BTP. [Data: Sources (3605, 3606), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 25), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## Security Updates and Reminders\n\nSAP BTP has issued several security updates and reminders, including the deprecation of weak client certificate chains, the removal of .NET, Ruby, and R buildpacks, and the addition of new IP addresses for Amazon Web Services regions. These updates aim to strengthen the security and compliance of SAP BTP's infrastructure and ensure that users are aware of potential security risks. [Data: Sources (3951, 3952, 3953), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 02), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## Authorization and Trust Management Service Updates\n\nThe Authorization and Trust Management Service has introduced new features, including the ability to manage API credentials and the limits for roles, role collections, trust, and service broker instances. These updates aim to improve the security and compliance of SAP BTP's authorization and trust management processes. [Data: Sources (3956, 3611), Date_Range ((2023, 12, 04), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Updates\n\nSAP Build Process Automation has introduced new features, including the Environment view, which lists SAP Build Process Automation projects by environment, and the ability to deploy projects in different shared environments. These updates aim to improve the efficiency and effectiveness of process automation within SAP BTP. [Data: Sources (3613, 3614, 3615), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 25), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Advanced Edition Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone Advanced Edition has introduced new features, including enhanced email notification domains, new wizard layouts in workspaces, and access levels for non-members. These updates aim to improve the user experience and efficiency of work zone operations within SAP BTP. [Data: Sources (3616, 3617, 3618, 3619), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 18), (2024, 01, 25))]", "# SAP BTP Community Overview as of 2023-11-30\n\nThis report provides an overview of the SAP BTP community, highlighting key entities, their relationships, and significant updates as of 2023-11-30. The community's structure, core attributes, and connections are discussed, along with noteworthy claims and their impact on the community.\n\n## SAP BTP's Operational Scope\n\nSAP BTP offers a wide range of services and features, including cloud infrastructure, data management, and security. Its operational scope is vast, covering various industries and business functions. The platform's flexibility and scalability make it an attractive choice for organizations looking to digitalize their operations. [Data: Sources (526, 722, 2137), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 30), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## Security Updates and Hardening\n\nSAP BTP has implemented several security updates and hardening measures to strengthen its platform. The deprecation of weak client certificate chains and the raising of OpenSSL security levels to 2 are notable examples. These changes aim to improve the overall security posture of the platform and protect against potential threats. [Data: Sources (526, 722, 2137), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 30), (2024, 02, 22))]\n\n## New Features and Functionality\n\nSAP BTP has introduced several new features and functionality, including the addition of new languages for the SAP digital payments add-on, the deprecation of weak client certificate chains, and the introduction of new IP addresses for SAP BTP regions. These updates aim to enhance the user experience and improve the overall functionality of the platform. [Data: Sources (526, 722, 2137), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 30), (2024, 02, 22))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key components and their interactions, highlighting the importance of technology in maintaining the platform's stability and user experience. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates and Enhancements\n\nCloud Foundry has been updated from 44.5.0 to 44.9.0, providing various enhancements and bug fixes. This update has improved the platform's stability and user experience. Effective updates and enhancements not only prevent technical issues but also support the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (2, 4), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## SAP Document AI Enhancements\n\nSAP Document AI has been improved with enhanced instant learning, new extraction methods for templates, and improved machine learning models for invoices, purchase orders, and payment advice. These enhancements have improved the platform's document processing capabilities, making it more efficient and accurate. [Data: Sources (6, 7, 8), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## SAP Secure Login Service and Alert Notifications\n\nSAP Secure Login Service now provides alert notifications for critical issues, such as problems with certificate subjects and custom certificate authority communication. This feature has improved the platform's security and user experience. [Data: Sources (9), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 12), (2025, 03, 06))]\n\n## Job Scheduling Service Enhancements\n\nThe Job Scheduling Service has been enhanced with new features, such as integration with SAP Cloud ALM and new Horizon themes in the user interface. These enhancements have improved the platform's job scheduling capabilities, making it more efficient and user-friendly. [Data: Sources (11, 12), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 29), (2025, 05, 29))]\n\n## Availability Service Enhancements\n\nThe Availability Service has been enhanced with improved accessibility, API documentation, and email performance. These enhancements have improved the platform's availability and user experience. [Data: Sources (13, 14, 15), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 29), (2025, 05, 29))]", "# SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Connectivity Overview as of November 2023\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Connectivity, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates. The information is relevant to the SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime and Connectivity operations around November 2023.\n\n## TLS 1.2 Cipher-Block-Chaining Ciphers Removal\n\nThe SAP BTP Cloud Foundry Runtime has removed TLS 1.2 Cipher-Block-Chaining (CBC) Ciphers from the environment for the region eu20. This change affects older clients and requires them to support one of the remaining TLS 1.2 ciphers to maintain connectivity. The removal of deprecated ciphers helps prevent potential security vulnerabilities and ensures compliance with evolving security standards. [Data: Sources (466), Date_Range ((2023, 10, 19), (2023, 11, 16))]\n\n## Cloud Connector Updates\n\nThe Cloud Connector has received several updates, including bug fixes and enhancements. The version 2.16.1 release addresses issues such as LDAP role name display, password handling, and subaccount selection. Additionally, the release introduces new features like sorting subaccount entries in the dashboard. These updates improve the overall performance and usability of the Cloud Connector, ensuring a smoother experience for users. [Data: Sources (467, 468, 469), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 16), (2024, 01, 01))]\n\n## Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nThe Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry have received updates, including bug fixes and improvements. The release adds MTA metadata attributes to user-provided service instances and preserves app environment after blue-green deployment. Additionally, the release improves performance and usability of deployment with MTA archive URL. These updates enhance the overall experience for users and improve the stability of the Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry. [Data: Sources (470, 471), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 06), (2023, 11, 16))]", "# SAP Cloud Identity Services Overview as of November 2023\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Identity Services, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to the company's technology operations around November 2023.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Component Overview\n\nSAP Cloud Identity Services consists of several key components, including Cloud Identity Services, Identity Provisioning, Kyma Runtime, and UI Theme Designer. These components operate in various environments such as Cloud Foundry, Kyma, and Neo. Each component plays a vital role in managing identity and access, provisioning, and runtime services. Effective management of these components ensures seamless integration and compliance with regulatory standards. [Data: Sources (422, 423), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 08), (2023, 11, 07))]\n\n## Regular Upgrades and Updates\n\nRegular upgrades and updates are essential for maintaining the integrity and security of SAP Cloud Identity Services. Recent updates include the upgrade of Identity Authentication, the introduction of SAP Initiated system type, and the update of Keda module to version 1.0.0. These updates ensure that the services remain compliant with the latest standards and regulations. [Data: Sources (422, 423, 425), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 08), (2023, 12, 06))]\n\n## Edge Integration Cell Updates\n\nEdge Integration Cell is a hybrid integration runtime offered as part of SAP Integration Suite. Recent updates include the general availability of Edge Integration Cell, sizing guidelines, and the introduction of custom sender adapters. These updates enable users to manage APIs and run integration scenarios within their private landscape. [Data: Sources (427, 428, 429), Date_Range ((2023, 11, 07), (2023, 11, 07))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of November 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their operational scope, core attributes, connections, and noteworthy claims. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around November 2024.\n\n## SAP Build Process Automation Operational Scope\n\nThe SAP Build Process Automation component at SAP plays a pivotal role in automating business processes. Their proactive approach, highlighted from the beginning of 2024, helps safeguard SAP against potential operational pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving technological standards. Effective process automation not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (791, 1980), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 11, 12))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services and Governance\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services component ensures that all SAP's operations adhere to the technological standards set by regulatory bodies. Their focus on identity management and directory services, noted starting November 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP's reputation and operational legality, especially in managing complex identities and access control. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high technological standards and security practices. [Data: Source (1974), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 01), (2024, 11, 12))]\n\n## Interdepartmental Collaboration for Compliance\n\nCollaboration between the SAP Build Process Automation and Cloud Identity Services components, established in November 2024, ensures that process automation strategies are technologically sound and that compliance measures consider identity management. This synergy is vital for holistic governance and has been instrumental in integrating process automation with identity management strategies at SAP. Enhanced interdepartmental cooperation during this period plays a crucial role in aligning the company's strategies with technological requirements. [Data: Sources (791, 1974), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 01), (2024, 11, 12))]\n\n## SAP Build Apps and Mobile Support\n\nThe SAP Build Apps component at SAP has discontinued support for Android devices with 32-bit processors, as announced in November 2024. This change aims to improve the file sizes of these builds and align with modern technological standards. The application preview for 32-bit devices remains supported. [Data: Source (1979), Date_Range ((2024, 11, 06), (2024, 11, 12))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime and Telemetry Module\n\nThe Kyma Runtime component at SAP has introduced a new version of the Telemetry module, version 1.26.0, as announced in November 2024. This update brings improvements to metrics, traces, and logs, ensuring that the company's operations are aligned with modern technological standards. [Data: Source (1978), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 23), (2024, 11, 12))]"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_0a7a9f02d81f6a9cf14aeadb4596103f0f7dcb83e94b742e304630c9ee310f36_v2"}